1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:16,000
Open the Prentice Files file at the window of the picture.

2
00:00:16,000 --> 00:00:24,000
Find the eFixition.a Simulation Instability the Entire Gamut file.

3
00:00:24,000 --> 00:00:30,000
Find the eFixition.a Simulation Instability the Entire Gamut file.

4
00:00:30,000 --> 00:00:33,000
Drag it to the 2D or 3D window.

5
00:00:33,000 --> 00:00:39,000
After the fire simulation, the panels will collide with each other immediately, causing the costume to move continuously.

6
00:00:39,000 --> 00:00:43,000
This is because the panel is not in the correct position when it is arranged.

7
00:00:47,000 --> 00:00:52,000
In the 3D window, select Rearrange 3D Arrangement, All.

8
00:00:52,000 --> 00:00:59,000
In the 3D window, the panels will be remodeled before the simulation.

9
00:01:08,000 --> 00:01:11,000
In the 2D window, select the front panel panel.

10
00:01:11,000 --> 00:01:17,000
In the 3D window, right-click and select Rearrange 2D Position Arrangement.

11
00:01:17,000 --> 00:01:22,000
Select the 2D arrangement of the front panel to the 3D window.

12
00:01:22,000 --> 00:01:25,000
In the 3D window, right-click on the panel.

13
00:01:25,000 --> 00:01:27,000
Left-click to select the positional ball.

14
00:01:27,000 --> 00:01:31,000
Use the quick arrangement tool to arrange the panels to the front panel.

15
00:01:31,000 --> 00:01:34,000
Use the positional ball tool to arrange the panels to the inside of the panel.

16
00:01:34,000 --> 00:01:36,000
Repeat the operation on the other side.

17
00:01:36,000 --> 00:01:39,000
Place the panels behind the front panel panel.

18
00:01:43,000 --> 00:01:48,000
In the 2D window, select the right-front panel and the right-front panel panel.

19
00:01:48,000 --> 00:01:51,000
In the 3D window, use the positional ball tool.

20
00:01:51,000 --> 00:01:54,000
Place the right-front panel to the top of the left-front panel.

21
00:01:54,000 --> 00:01:57,000
Rotate the view to see the distance between the panels.

22
00:02:06,000 --> 00:02:07,000
Open the arrangement point.

23
00:02:07,000 --> 00:02:10,000
In the 2D window, select the front panel panel.

24
00:02:11,000 --> 00:02:15,000
In the front window arrangement point, click to put the panel down.

25
00:02:15,000 --> 00:02:19,000
In the 2D window, select the outer panel panel.

26
00:02:19,000 --> 00:02:24,000
In the 3D window, use the positional ball tool to drag the outer panel away from the inner panel.

27
00:02:24,000 --> 00:02:27,000
Rotate the view to see the distance between the panels.

28
00:02:27,000 --> 00:02:31,000
In the 2D window, select the outer panel of the lower right panel.

29
00:02:31,000 --> 00:02:36,000
In the 3D window, use the positional ball tool to drag the panel away from the left panel.

30
00:02:36,000 --> 00:02:39,000
Rotate the view to see the distance between the panels.

31
00:02:43,000 --> 00:02:44,000
Activate the simulation.

32
00:02:44,000 --> 00:02:47,000
Check if the clothing can be stabilized.

33
00:02:47,000 --> 00:02:49,000
Turn off the simulation.

